WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.817
Heidi arrived in Grandmamma's room and looked with delight at the beautiful and colorful books.

2
00:00:05.818 --> 00:00:09.475
She sat beside Grandmamma and eagerly turned the pages.

3
00:00:09.476 --> 00:00:13.058
Halfway through one book, she suddenly cried out.

4
00:00:13.059 --> 00:00:18.550
For a moment or two, she looked at the picture with happy eyes, and then, she burst into sobs.

5
00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:22.050
Grandmamma looked at the picture that was upsetting Heidi.

6
00:00:22.051 --> 00:00:27.070
It was a green pasture with young animals grazing on the fresh grass.

7
00:00:27.071 --> 00:00:31.833
In the middle was a shepherd leaning on his staff and looking at his happy flock.

8
00:00:31.834 --> 00:00:38.356
The whole scene was bathed in golden light because the sun was just sinking below the horizon.

9
00:00:38.357 --> 00:00:43.987
"Don't cry, dear child, don't cry," said Grandmamma.

10
00:00:43.988 --> 00:00:47.578
"The picture has reminded you of something, I think.

11
00:00:47.579 --> 00:00:51.605
But there is a beautiful story that goes with it."

12
00:00:51.606 --> 00:00:58.715
Since the day that Heidi had tried to go home and Fraulein had taken Grannie's rolls, a change had come over Heidi.

13
00:00:58.716 --> 00:01:02.925
She realized now that she could not go home whenever she wanted.

14
00:01:02.926 --> 00:01:07.056
She would have to stay in Frankfurt for a long time─maybe forever.

15
00:01:07.057 --> 00:01:16.297
Even though Clara, Herr Sesemann, Grandmamma, and even Sebastian were kind to her, Heidi's life with them was making her sad.

16
00:01:16.298 --> 00:01:24.476
But Heidi worried that Herr Sesemann would think she was ungrateful if she wanted to leave, and so would Grandmamma and Clara as well.

17
00:01:24.477 --> 00:01:29.038
There was no one she could talk to about her longing to go home.

18
00:01:29.039 --> 00:01:33.594
As days passed, the weight grew heavier and heavier on Heidi's heart.

19
00:01:33.595 --> 00:01:37.978
She ate less and less, and every day she grew a little paler.

20
00:01:37.979 --> 00:01:43.653
She was awake for long hours in the night picturing the mountain with its sunshine and flowers.

21
00:01:43.654 --> 00:01:49.310
When she finally fell asleep, she would dream of the mountains turning a soft red in the evening light.

22
00:01:49.311 --> 00:01:52.835
She would wake up in the morning thinking that she was back at the hut.

23
00:01:52.836 --> 00:02:02.965
And when she suddenly realized that she was far from home, she would lay her face in her pillow and weep quietly so that no one could hear.

24
00:02:02.966 --> 00:02:06.555
Heidi's unhappiness did not escape Grandmamma's notice.

25
00:02:06.556 --> 00:02:08.620
She watched Heidi carefully.

26
00:02:08.621 --> 00:02:15.050
After a few days, when she realized that Heidi was getting more and more sad, she took her into her room.

27
00:02:15.051 --> 00:02:20.450
"Now, tell me, Heidi, what is the matter?" she asked.

28
00:02:20.451 --> 00:02:23.039
"Are you in trouble?"

29
00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:26.465
But Heidi was afraid to tell Grandmamma the truth.

30
00:02:26.466 --> 00:02:29.744
"I can't tell you," she said simply.

31
00:02:29.745 --> 00:02:34.939
"Well, could you tell Clara about it?" asked Grandmamma.

32
00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:37.957
"Oh, no, I cannot tell anyone,"

33
00:02:37.958 --> 00:02:47.235
said Heidi in so firm a tone and with such a troubled look on her face that Grandmamma felt a deep pity for the child.

34
00:02:47.237 --> 00:02:52.155
"Then, dear child, let me tell you what to do.

35
00:02:52.156 --> 00:02:57.312
When we are in great trouble, we must pray to God for help.

36
00:02:57.313 --> 00:03:00.918
You say your prayers every evening, don't you?"

37
00:03:00.919 --> 00:03:05.801
"No, I never say any prayers," answered Heidi.

38
00:03:05.802 --> 00:03:10.568
"Have you never been taught to pray?" Grandmamma said with surprise.

39
00:03:10.569 --> 00:03:14.917
"You think no one can help you, but it is not true.

40
00:03:14.918 --> 00:03:20.335
When your heart is heavy with grief, you can tell everything to God.

41
00:03:20.336 --> 00:03:23.156
He can help make you happy again."

42
00:03:23.157 --> 00:03:26.492
A sudden gleam of joy came into Heidi's eyes,

43
00:03:26.493 --> 00:03:29.311
"May I tell Him everything?"

44
00:03:29.312 --> 00:03:33.681
"Yes, of course," was Grandmamma's answer.

45
00:03:33.682 --> 00:03:36.593
Quickly, Heidi ran to her own room.

46
00:03:36.594 --> 00:03:43.242
She sat down on her chair, closed her eyes, and told God everything that was making her so sad and unhappy.

47
00:03:43.243 --> 00:03:51.430
She begged God earnestly to help her and to let her go home to Grandfather.

